    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41146" root="هرش" body-key="h">
    
      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَارَشَا</span></b>  [<i>They fought and assailed each other</i>]:
said of two dogs. (A.) See also 6. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلْبُ هِرَاشٍ</span> [<i>An irritable,</i> or <i>a quarrelsome, dog</i>];
like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلْبُ خِرَاشٍ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also 2. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِرَاشٌ</span>
is also used to signify The <i>fighting against each
other</i> of men. (Mgh.)

